From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] userenv: the environment block names an account with a domain (5971)

CreateEnvironmentBlock looked the token's account up with no buffer for its
domain, which fails (ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER) for every account that has
one: the block then had no USERNAME or USERPROFILE unless a ProfileList
entry or the Volatile Environment supplied them, and the user's TEMP
("%USERPROFILE%\AppData\Local\Temp") stayed unexpanded. A shared prefix's
users have neither; the shell, reading its environment again after an
installer's broadcast, handed that TEMP to every program it started.
Gate test/envreload-gate.sh (mutant CEB_NO_DOMAIN).
---
--- a/dlls/userenv/userenv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/userenv/userenv_main.c
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@
     {
         TOKEN_USER *token_user = NULL;
         SID_NAME_USE use;
-        WCHAR *sidW;
+        WCHAR *sidW, domain[256];
         DWORD size, tmp=0;
 
         if (GetTokenInformation(hToken, TokenUser, NULL, 0, &len) ||
@@ -313,8 +313,24 @@
         memcpy(buf, profiles_dir, len*sizeof(WCHAR));
 
         size = UNICODE_STRING_MAX_CHARS-len;
+        /* Stained Glass OS: with no buffer for the account's domain the lookup
+         * fails (ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER) for every account that has one --
+         * the block then had no USERNAME or USERPROFILE, unless a ProfileList
+         * entry gave the profile, and TEMP stayed "%USERPROFILE%\...": the
+         * shell's environment, read again after an installer's broadcast,
+         * handed that to every program it started, and Prism Launcher exited
+         * at once (qa4, a shared prefix's users have no ProfileList entry) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_CEB_NO_DOMAIN
+        tmp = ARRAY_SIZE(domain);
+#endif
         if (LookupAccountSidW(NULL, token_user->User.Sid,
-                    buf+len, &size, NULL, &tmp, &use))
+                    buf+len, &size,
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_CEB_NO_DOMAIN
+                    domain,
+#else
+                    NULL,
+#endif
+                    &tmp, &use))
         {
             set_env_var(&env, L"USERNAME", buf+len);
             if (len) set_env_var(&env, L"USERPROFILE", buf);
